This article lists the presidents of [[Balboa]] since the country's reunification in 1973. Balboan presidential terms are formally five years, but the dates below reflect the main administrations in office; several presidents served shortened or extended periods because of early elections, caretaker arrangements, or the timing of constitutional transitions.

The last president of the rump state was [[Darío Caballero]], who served from 1968 to 1973. He oversaw the negotiations that completed reunification, but the office below begins with the first post-reunification administration.

